Z||000003||mrfixit58||04-24-2000||10:20 AM||||Well, I didn't do too bad. I had a little over $1000 invested including the purchase price of the car. I sold it to my Bro-In-Law for $2000. I'm still not sure I did the right thing. The car was a cream-puff and I'm not too sure I can replace it for the dollars sold. All the hard-to-get stuff was in real good shape (perfect dash, surrounds, door panels and carpet. Never been wreaked, strong motor with no smoke, etc.).<P>But never fear... I'm still on target to aquire a Yellow 88 GT w/ T-tops (sometime this year... when the lady is ready). And, I'm about to buy about 2 1/2 cars from a guy who wants to get rid of all his Fieros and parts (I'll have lots of parts to sell). I'll post more on the parts and parts cars when the deal is done and I've had time to sort through all the cars.<P>Still bummed but feeling better,<BR>Roy||||reg||2
Z||000004||Racer 1||04-24-2000||01:45 PM||||A few years back I sold my 1968 chevy malibu to my friend. He treated it like Krap tore the headliner and just tore the car up. Every time I saw the car it really hurt me to see it in such sad shape. I still feel bad about the deal. Just make sure your brother treats it good!!||||reg||9
Z||000005||mrfixit58||04-24-2000||04:00 PM||||My Bro-in-law is a unique person. He will throw a lot of money into the car to make it really nice, then he'll drive the crap out of it. When he's tired of it (or when he breaks it bad enough that his neighbor buddys won't work on it any more), he'll want to unload it cheap. If he doesn't wreak it, and it still looks good, maybe I can buy it back for half of what I sold it to him for and then slip in that 3.4 or 3800 SC I've been dreaming about...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Roy||||reg||1
